  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 257 PM CDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\nThe front continues southward on Thursday, and eventually drier air \nmoves in, ending the precip across southeast Missouri by 00Z Friday. \n Weak high pressure builds into the Upper Midwest and Great Lakes \nThursday night into Friday which will produce dry and relatively \ncooler weather for Friday.  However another short wave trough moves \nacross the Midwest in quasi-zonal flow aloft Friday night into \nSaturday.  This pushes another cold front with another round of \nconvection into Iowa Friday night, and the front stalls over \nnorthern Missouri on Saturday.  The front and any outflow boundaries \nthat overnight convection produces will provide a focus for \nscattered convection Saturday afternoon, though drier low level air \nlingering ahead of the front looks like it will keep the atmosphere \nfrom becoming too unstable.  A chance for showers and thunderstorms \ncontinues Sunday into next week as a strong short wave trough moves \nfrom the Intermountain West across the Northern Plains.  This forces \nlow level cyclogenesis over the Plains and turns the low level flow \nover the Mid Mississippi Valley back to the southwest. Temperatures \nremain 5-10 degrees above normal in the mid 80s to low 90s through \nthe end of the forecast period due to the persistent southwest flow.",
